Network Backbone Summary
Hardware: Dual ASUS RT-BE88U in AiMesh with a 10GbE wired backhaul. A TP-Link TL-SX1008 is between the two units. 
Logic: High-performance tasks (Photogrammetry/Compute) are partitioned to Asgardr or Wired connections. Legacy and low-priority peripherals are relegated to Midgardr.

Hardware Logic & Constraints
Odinn Networking [LOCKED]: Onboard Marvell 5GbE is the terminal velocity. PCIe lanes are fully allocated to dual RDNA 4 GPUs (x8/x8). No NIC expansion possible.

Iðavöllr I/O: Connected via Thunderbolt 4. The 2.5GbE port on the CalDigit TS4 is recognized but considered a secondary interface to prevent bus contention with the primary 5GbE link.

IP Segmentation: Distribution is categorized by Device Class: .0 Backbone/Infrastructure, .50 IoT, .100 Desktops, .150 Laptops, .200 Printers, .250 Mobile. 

Infrastructure Note: WAN is capped at 1Gbps/50Mbps. The 10GbE internal backbone (TL-SX1008) exists solely to facilitate the AiMesh backhaul and future-proof internal lateral transfers between Yggdrasill/Laeradr nodes. Likewise, the 1GbE thread exists solely to provide power and data to PoE devices. We have four spare non-PoE slots there if we need them, however.

Naming Logic
INFRASTRUCTURE
Yggdrasill: ASUS RT-BE88U (Primary Router) - The network that contains all the machines. Therefore, it is the world tree. The port to the outside is named Bifrost in the router but doesn't really do anything naming wise within the network framework.
Laeradr: ASUS RT-BE88U (AiMesh Node) - The "crown" of Yggdrasil. It is part of it, but separate, just as the AI node is part of the network but not the primary router.
Mimameidr: TP-Link TL-SX1008 (Backhaul Bridge) - This is the switch that connects the two RT-BE88U routers. As such, it is part of Yggdrasill even though it does not have a formal IP.
Valgrind: TP-LInk TL-SG608P (PoE Switch) This switch exists to provide PoE connections to devices that do not have sufficient power otherwise. As such, it is part of Yggdrasill as a network but leads to Valholl
Valholl: SMLIGHT SLZB-06MG24U (Matter router) - If Bifrost is the connection to the outside world, then Valholl is the connection to the world of IoT devices via Matter. Since these devices lack computational power (soul) and do not have IPs (bodies) they are mapped to the Einherjar. See separate manifest.
Bilrost: Galaxy S21 - the former Hermodr. It is the connection to the world when the main connection fails. As such, it is the fleeting bridge, not Bifrost.

